      "writtenOn": "2025-10-23T18:26:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This function might get called by 2 times for each gop:\n\nThe first run is with gop_eval \u003e 0, to see if we want to use max gop size \u003e16 or \u003c\u003d16. \n\nIf it is decided we should use gop_size \u003e 16, then the stats from the first run is used. \n\nIf it is decided we should use gop_size \u003c\u003d 16, then we will need to run this function with gop_eval \u003d 0 again. \n\nI think this is correctly handled in the current CL since we will erase the last run\u0027s data with `init_tpl_stats_before_propagation`. But still pointing this out in case.",
